 "notes": "1916 flats, six storeys. Buff brick uppers with five brown-painted splayed bays from the first upper storey to the roof, a railed steel fire escape right of centre, window pairs between; tall orange-brown brick ground storey with a three-part window left, a gated entry with a transom, two small windows and a shopfront at the right end. Brown trim, deep brown cornice. Rework r-eddy: arched surround on the iron gate, higher sills so the ground windows read as small high lights. Tint lift (2026-10-02): paint tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k); brick tints converted to target / kit colour.",
